{"hey":{"w":"hey","zh":["喂","哎","嗨","嘿"],"ipa":{"uk":"/heɪ/","us":"/heɪ/"},"ety":[{"n":1,"chain":[{"l":"enm","f":"hey","t":"inh"},{"l":"ang","f":"*hē","t":"inh"}],"text":"From Middle English hey, hei, also without h- in ey, from Old English *hē, ēa (interjection), attested as first element in hēlā, ēalā (“O!, alas!, oh!, lo!”). Cognate with Dutch hé, hei (“hi, hey”), German hei (“hey, wow”), Danish and Swedish hej (“hello, hey”), Faroese hey (“hey, hello”), Old Norse, Icelandic and Norwegian hei (“hey”), Polish hej (“hey, hello”), Romanian hei, Russian эй (ej, “hey”); see heigh.","cog":[{"l":"nl","f":"hé"},{"l":"de","f":"hei"},{"l":"da","f":"-"},{"l":"sv","f":"hej"},{"l":"fo","f":"hey"},{"l":"non","f":"-"},{"l":"is","f":"-"},{"l":"no","f":"hei"}]},{"n":2,"chain":[{"l":"fr","f":"haie","t":"der","g":"hedge"},{"l":"frm","f":"haye","t":"inh"},{"l":"fro","f":"haie","t":"inh"},{"l":"la-med","f":"haga","t":"der"},{"l":"frk","f":"*haggju","t":"der"}],"text":"From French haie (“hedge”), with reference to the weaving patterns used in hedgelaying. Doublet of hedge and quay."}],"pos":[{"p":"intj","e":0,"senses":[{"d":"An exclamation to get attention.","tags":["informal"],"ex":["Hey, look at this!","Hey! Listen!"],"syn":["oi"],"grp":0,"zh":"喂；哎；嗨"},{"d":"A protest or reprimand.","tags":["informal"],"ex":["Hey! Stop that!"],"grp":1},{"d":"An expression of surprise.","tags":["informal"],"ex":["Hey! This is new!"],"syn":["blimey"],"grp":2},{"d":"An informal greeting, similar to hi.","tags":["informal"],"ex":["Hey! How's it going?"],"syn":["hi"],"grp":3,"zh":"嗨"},{"d":"A request for repetition or explanation; an expression of confusion.","tags":["informal"],"ex":["Hey? How's that?"],"syn":["eh","huh"],"grp":4},{"d":"Used as a tag question, to emphasise what goes before or to request that the listener express an opinion about what has been said.","tags":["informal"],"ex":["\"Who 's a cur - now - hey?\""],"grp":4},{"d":"A meaningless beat marker or extra, filler syllable in song lyrics.","tags":["informal"],"ex":["The chorus is \"nana na na, nana na na hey hey hey, goodbye\"."],"grp":5}]},{"p":"verb","e":0,"senses":[{"d":"To greet with a \"hey\"","tags":["informal"]}],"forms":[["3s","heys"],["ing","heying"],["pp","heyed"],["past","heyed"]]},{"p":"noun","e":1,"senses":[{"d":"A choreographic figure in which three or more dancers weave between one another, passing by left and right shoulder alternately.","tags":["informal","sports"]}],"forms":[["pl","heys"]]}],"grp":[{"label":"exclamation to get attention","zh":["喂","哎","嗨","嘿"],"p":"intj","e":0,"tr":{"fr":["fr:hé"],"it":["it:ehi","it:ou"],"es":["es:imperative oír","es:hey","es:ey"],"pt":["pt:ei"]}},{"label":"protest or reprimand","zh":[],"p":"intj","e":0,"tr":{"fr":["fr:hé"],"it":["it:ehi"],"es":["es:imperative oír","es:hey","es:ey"],"pt":["pt:ei","pt:epa","pt:opa"]}},{"label":"expression of surprise","zh":[],"p":"intj","e":0,"tr":{"fr":["fr:holà"],"it":[],"es":["es:hey","es:ey","es:eh"],"pt":["pt:epa","pt:opa"]}},{"label":"informal greeting","zh":["嗨"],"p":"intj","e":0,"tr":{"fr":["fr:coucou"],"it":[],"es":["es:hey","es:ey","es:eh"],"pt":["pt:oi","pt:e aí"]}},{"label":"request for repetition or explanation","zh":[],"p":"intj","e":0,"tr":{"fr":[],"it":[],"es":["es:hey","es:ey","es:eh"],"pt":["pt:hã","pt:hem"]}},{"label":"meaningless beat marker, filler syllable","zh":[],"p":"intj","e":0,"tr":{"fr":[],"it":[],"es":[],"pt":["pt:é","pt:hey"]}}],"lx":{"fr:hé":{"w":"hé","p":"intj","ipa":"/e/","gl":"Used to call someone; hey","ety":{"chain":[]}},"it:ehi":{"w":"ehi","p":"intj","ipa":"/ˈej/","gl":"hey! (used to attract someone's attention)","ety":{"chain":[]}},"it:ou":{"w":"ou","p":"intj","gl":"used to get someone's attention; oi, hey","ety":{"chain":[]}},"es:imperative oír":{"w":"imperative oír"},"es:hey":{"w":"hey","p":"intj","ipa":"/ˈei/","gl":"hey!","ety":{"chain":[{"l":"en","f":"hey","t":"bor"}],"text":"Unadapted borrowing from English hey."}},"es:ey":{"w":"ey","p":"intj","ipa":"/ˈei/","gl":"hey!","e